# Best practices

React 19 + Vite, JavaScript (JSX), plain CSS. Follow the existing file layout under `src/`.

## Components

- Functional components only. One component per file when it has its own markup or state.
- Keep `App.jsx` thin. Put feature UI in `src/components/` and shared logic in `src/hooks/`.
- Name components in PascalCase, files to match (`SearchForm.jsx`). Hooks start with `use`.
- Derive values during render. Use state only for values that change over time.
- Colocate CSS with the component (`SearchForm.jsx` + `SearchForm.css`) instead of growing `App.css`.

```jsx
// Prefer
function MemberCard({ name, city }) {
  return (
    <article className="member-card">
      <h2>{name}</h2>
      <p>{city}</p>
    </article>
  )
}

// Avoid inline objects and anonymous handlers in lists
members.map((member) => (
  <MemberCard key={member.id} member={member} onSelect={handleSelect} />
))
```

## Data and effects

- Fetch in `useEffect` only when there is no event handler to put it in. Cancel or ignore stale responses.
- Handle loading, empty, and error states in the UI. Do not swallow errors.
- Do not add libraries (routers, state, UI kits) unless the task needs them. This app starts with React only.

## JavaScript

- ES modules. No unused variables (ESLint: `no-unused-vars`, ignore `^[A-Z_]`).
- Prefer `const`. Name booleans as questions (`isLoading`, `hasResults`).
- Guard early. Return null or a small empty state instead of deep nested JSX.

## CSS

- Class names in kebab-case, scoped to the component (`.member-card`, `.member-card-title`).
- Put shared tokens (`--color-primary`, spacing, radius) on `:root` in `index.css`. Reuse them.
- Mobile first. Add `@media (min-width: …)` for larger screens. Current content max width is `1200px`.
